        "reference": "3 Nephi 10:11",
        "book": "3 Nephi",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And it was the more righteous part of the people who were saved, and it was they who received the prophets and stoned them not; and it was they who had not shed the blood of the saints, who were spared—",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "2 Ne. 26:8; 3 Ne. 9:13 (11–13); 27:31."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "3 Nephi 10:12",
        "book": "3 Nephi",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And they were spared and were not sunk and buried up in the earth; and they were not drowned in the depths of the sea; and they were not burned by fire, neither were they fallen upon and crushed to death; and they were not carried away in the whirlwind; neither were they overpowered by the vapor of smoke and of darkness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "3 Nephi 10:13",
        "book": "3 Nephi",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
